  - title: A display to beat the tower
    number: 6
    heartsNeeded: 6
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Here's my plan. The tower sells pictures of doors. I'm going to build a real one right in the window. Oak, brass hinges, the works.
    - People can open it, close it, knock on it. Let's see a box do that!
    - I need good timber, though. Would you bring me some wood?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 74774f685447bd4458cd1bed839c572e, type: 2}
      amount: 20
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: Timber for Frank's window
      questText: Frank wants 20 Wood to build a real door in his shop window, to beat the tower's flat-pack doors.
      reminder:
      - How's the wood coming? Twenty pieces and I can start tonight. I don't sleep much anyway. Ha.
      thanks:
      - Now THAT is timber. Smell that!
      - Come back in a few days. That door is going to be the best thing on Shop Street.
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The bank letter
    number: 7
    heartsNeeded: 7
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Emeka brought a letter this morning. He looked like he was delivering it to a funeral.
    - The bank. The store's loan. Three months to pay, or they take the building.
    - And a man from Sterling turned up an hour later, like he'd been waiting round the corner. He made me an offer. A fair one, too. That's the worst part.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Frank's choice
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Gus has an idea. A co-op, he calls it. Everybody on the street buys a share of the store. Walt, the Kims, Marcus, Gus. You.
    - It'd still be Frank's. Just... Frank's and everybody's. I'd have to let people tell me what to do. Walt would tell me what to do. Every day.
    - Or I take Sterling's money, pay the bank, buy a little house, and sleep in a real bed. You tell me. I'm too close to see it straight.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Make it a co-op
      replyA:
      - A co-op. Frank's and everybody's.
      - Walt's going to make me put the screws in alphabetical order. I can feel it. All right. All right! Let's do it.
      flagsA:
      - frank_coop
      optionB: Sell to Sterling
      replyB:
      - Sell. Yeah. Yeah, that's the sensible thing.
      - Thirty-one years. I'll sign on Monday. Don't tell Gus yet. Let me tell Gus.
      flagsB:
      - frank_sold_store
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Frank's and everybody's
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Fifteen shares sold in a week! Rosa bought one with her egg money. Nia bought one with her pocket money, so now I've got a nine-year-old on the board.
    - Walt reorganised the screws. Gus stands at the door and tells everybody my prices are robbery, then sends them in.
    - Saturday mornings we're running workshops. Fix your own tap. Hang your own door. Thirty people last week!
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
